      "writtenOn": "2022-12-12T23:30:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note: while this direct macro approach of using Perfetto is only used on Android, then if someone starts tracing to a new category not defined here, it will result in a compilation error that won\u0027t be caught until the next Android roll. Does this seem like a blocker, or just something to notify folks about during the transition phase?",
      "revId": "6fa2afe4254aefe5291dac050f63829022de6feb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04e202cd_e0dd89dd",
        "filename": "src/core/SkTraceEventCommon.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 5255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T21:31:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems fine to me. Some other options:\n- Make it happen automatically. I\u0027m guessing this doesn\u0027t work, or at least it\u0027s not clear how to make it work, though.\n- Make this a compilation error for *all* builds. Then it would be caught during development. I lean towards this, if it\u0027s not too hard.",
      "parentUuid": "c675a68c_7c4e7589",
      "revId": "6fa2afe4254aefe5291dac050f63829022de6feb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a142715_b33a3bde",
        "filename": "src/core/SkTraceEventCommon.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 19099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it will be possible to make it a compilation error for _some_ builds that will at least be exercised in Skia\u0027s presubmits, but it\u0027s actually a tricky enough situation that I\u0027m afraid to spend time on it at this moment. I\u0027ve filed b/262718654 as a fast follow (P1), will make an announcement warning folks, and also volunteer to be the one to handle adding them here if someone forgets and a roll breaks. Does that seem OK for now?",
