      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, there\u0027s apparently a slight cost to using any string that Perfetto doesn\u0027t know about at compile time.\n\nCallers using ::perfetto::DynamicString manually would require the caller to wrap their TRACE_EVENT call in #ifdef to check if Perfetto is actually present.\n\n(Sidenote: I was going to say this won\u0027t be necessary at the proposed stage 4 of go/skia-perfetto, but actually AFAIK we would still want to let some clients to opt out of Perfetto entirely (e.g. very size-sensitive clients that don\u0027t care about tracing), so we can\u0027t guarantee we have it.)",
      "parentUuid": "0d922f3e_96a2fe63",
      "revId": "6fa2afe4254aefe5291dac050f63829022de6feb",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
