      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That definitely seems nicer, but I\u0027m a little nervous about how that might play out in some edge cases:\n\nHWUI is built (in some capacity) for Windows in host mode. Often that will mean means cross-compiling from a Linux machine using MinGW, which is currently unsupported by Perfetto, so it\u0027s a scenario that we don\u0027t support here and would hit this `return false` case.\n\nI\u0027m unclear whether whatever HWUI is doing on Windows in host mode would hit the same code that will set this from a sysprop during HWUI\u0027s initialization, but I\u0027m skeptical enough of our \"Android framework stuff on Windows cross-compiled from Linux\" testing story to be a little nervous about doing a runtime abort here in that scenario. Though it\u0027s certainly possible I\u0027m misunderstanding the situation.\n\nWhat about a higher priority logging message, like a WARN or ERROR (if those are supported in Skia on Android)? Alternatively we could log a warning/error at the call site in HWUI if this returns false.",
      "parentUuid": "2f042ef5_87d168ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 227,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 227,
        "endChar": 16
