      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, this is to support the current `_ALWAYS` variants. I 100% agree we should eventually be using more granular categories instead of `_ALWAYS`, but I believe we need to keep this around during the transitionary stages(s). For two reasons:\n1. Most apps will still use ATrace at the start, and I don\u0027t want to impact the traces we get for random apps on bug reports (and the traces looked at by automated systems), which likely won\u0027t have the `debug.hwui.skia_atrace_enabled` sysprop enabled, so they\u0027ll be relying on `_ALWAYS`.\n2. This will allow for a fairer A/B performance comparison IMO.\n\nLeaving open to discuss, but see the proposed stages I just fleshed out on go/skia-perfetto",
