        "id": 19099
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have tests in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tests/TracingTest.cpp for our main/legacy-Chrome tracing system, but that\u0027s because our code is actually doing the heavy lifting in that case.\n\nOnce we give something to Perfetto, I trust that their own testing is plenty sufficient. The main area I was concerned about was the weird logic that used to be in `TRACE_EVENT_ATRACE_OR_PERFETTO_FORCEABLE`, but I\u0027ve since simplified that to be pretty straight-forward.\n\nI\u0027m also not sure what tests for these macros would look like. I\u0027m leaning towards omitting tests here, but I\u0027m happy to investigate more if you\u0027d like me to? Personally I think something closer to integration/end-to-end tests in Android-land would be a lot more helpful for us.",
