      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, it was some weird logic to handle routing `_ALWAYS` events to ATrace when \"overall\" / \"broad\" / \"all the things\" tracing (`setEnableTracing`) was OFF, but Perfetto was actually selected as the tracing backend.\n\nIn hindsight everything will be simpler and 1:1 comparisons will be easier if we just always route to the selected backend, regardless of `_ALWAYS` or `setEnableTracing`. So I\u0027ve reworked this logic and tweaked the Perfetto initialization logic to reflect that.\n\nI still believe we need `_ALWAYS` (and thus `force_always_trace`), but happy to reopen and discuss more.\n\nRelated: I\u0027ve also now added the `.always` suffix to category names used in `_ALWAYS` trace events. This is so we can selectively enable only these categories sometimes in Perfetto when doing 1:1 comparisons.",
